g/reductions/scheduling, we should use OpenMP pragmas.\n\nLet's craft solution:\n\n- Include <omp.h>? Not necessary for pragma but might be needed for omp_get_num_threads if used. We can just use `#pragma omp parallel for reduction(max:mxSum)`.\n- Use long long for sums and prefix.\n- Ensure we don't overflow in colPref; using long long.\n\nMemory optimization: Instead of storing full N x N column prefix, we could store only the needed vertical segment sums? But simpler to allocate vector<vector<long long>> colPref(n+1, vector<long long>(n)) maybe with n rows and n cols. Actually colPref[i][j] for i from 0..n-1; but we need access r+S-1 up to n-1, so fine.\n\nWe can compute colPref as:\nvector<vector<long long>> colPref(n, vector<long long>(n));\nfor j in 0..n-1:\n    long long running = 0;\n    for i in 0..n-1:\n        running += matrix[i][j];\n        colPref[i][j] = running;\n\nThen vertical sum from r to r+S-1 inclusive is colPref[r+S-1][j] - (r>0 ? colPref[r-1][j] : 0).\n\nWe'll use flat arrays for better cache? But vector of vectors okay.\n\nParallel loop:\nlong long mxSum = LLONG_MIN;\n#pragma omp parallel for reduction(max:mxSum) schedule(static)\nfor(int r=0; r<=n-s; ++r) {\n    // compute initial sum at c=0\n    long long cur = 0;\n    for(int c=0;c<s;++c) {\n        long long seg = colPref[r+s-1][c] - (r>0 ? colPref[r-1][c] : 0);\n        cur += seg;\n    }\n    if(cur > mxSum) mxSum = cur; // reduction handles\n    for(int c=1;c<=n-s;++c) {\n        int outCol = c-1;\n        int inCol = c+s-1;\n        long long segOut = colPref[r+s-1][outCol] - (r>0 ? colPref[r-1][outCol] : 0);\n        long long segIn = colPref[r+s-1][inCol] - (r>0 ? colPref[r-1][inCol] : 0);\n        cur += segIn - segOut;\n        if(cur > mxSum) mxSum = cur; // reduction\n    }\n}\n\nBut note: In OpenMP reduction, we should not manually update mxSum inside loop? Actually with `reduction(max:mxSum)` each thread has a private copy initialized to the identity (for max it's -infinity)